Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-157a: a jump to code from the Properties panel of
 a page that 0.140's layout closed no longer crashes; the real-VS-Code layer
 runs again; head-script forwarding pages (0.157.0, no version change)

Machine patch, found by running the real-VS-Code layer (test\vscode_it.ps1) on 0.157 for the first time since 0.79
(the pending VS Code update that blocked it is gone; VS Code 1.140):
- extension.js: panelColumn(d) -- a designer panel that is gone throws on .viewColumn ("Webview is disposed"); since
  0.140 a page closes itself when a C++ / .dfm file opens, so codeColumn / sourceColumn (every "jump to code / HTML")
  crashed for a page just closed. Now null = open beside.
- test\vscode_it.ps1: the test instance sets ht9045Designer.defaultView = design (its checks were written for the
  design-only / beside layout; 0.140's wpf layout needs checks of its own -- HANDOVER section 7); the default time
  limit 180 -> 600 s (159 checks take ~190 s; the instance was killed and no report written).
  Result here: 156 / 159 -- the 3 failing are the "Pages" list checks that 0.139 folded into the Solution Explorer.
- lib\pageinfo.js redirectTarget: a <head> script whose first statement is location.replace(...) forwards the page
  whatever its body holds (another session made Setup.Configuration.html and Setup.DIOInterFaceCFG.html forward to
  their Config.* pages, keeping the old body; the page list -- first 8 KB -- said forwarding, this said not, a lib
  check failed). Over every page only those two change.
HANDOVER section 7: the done items struck (TabOrder 0.152, Tab-order mode 0.156, toolbox groups 0.153), layer 4's state.
Tests: lib 179/179, probe 7/7 + tab tree 7/7, extension 219/219, panels all pass; real VS Code 156/159 (the 3 above).

